<section class="lp-band lp-planner" aria-labelledby="planner-title">
  <div class="lp-section lp-planner-grid">
    <div class="lp-intro">
      <h2 id="planner-title">Start with one sentence.</h2>
      <p>Tell the Planner what you’re organizing. It asks a few focused questions and builds the project: sign-ups, tasks, a schedule and a budget, as suggestions you keep or drop. It plans from the project details and never sees your people directory.</p>
      <%= link_to "More about planner", features_planner_path, class: "lp-feature-more" %>
    </div>
    <%= render "landing/scene", name: "tour-planner", width: 1100, height: 560, class: "lp-scene lp-float",
          alt: "The Planner: ‘Vacation Bible School, June 8 to 12, about 40 kids’ is typed in. Three questions follow: who VBS is for, what needs the most hands, and whether there is a budget. Each answer fills more of the preview, from the sign-up sheet to tasks, the schedule and the budget, and the project is added" %>
  </div>
</section>
